  "question": {
    "text": "From the base of a pole of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;meter, the angle of elevation of the top of a tower is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The pole subtends an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at the top of the tower. Then the height of the tower is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0007_ec7be4eeb568.png\" style=\"width: 308px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>So, height of tower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"
  }
}